⚡ CONCEPTUAL VIVA QUESTIONS
❓ What is abstract class?
👉 A class that cannot be instantiated and may contain abstract methods.
❓ Why use abstract class?
👉 To provide common structure and enforce method implementation.
❓ What is abstract method?
👉 A method without body that must be implemented in child class.
❓ Difference between abstract class and interface?
👉 Abstract class = partial implementation
👉 Interface = full abstraction
❓ What is polymorphism here?
👉 One Animal reference pointing to multiple child objects.
❓ What is runtime polymorphism?
👉 Method execution decided at runtime.
❓ What is method overriding?
👉 Child class redefining parent method.
❓ Why use Animal reference?
👉 To achieve flexibility and reduce code duplication.
❓ What is dynamic method dispatch?
👉 JVM decides which method to call at runtime.
❓ Why use Scanner?
👉 To take user input.
❓ Why use nextLine after nextInt?
👉 To clear buffer issue.
❓ What is real-world use?
👉 AI animal classification, game character systems, simulation software.
🧠 FINAL ONE-LINE SUMMARY
“This program demonstrates abstraction using abstract class Animal, where multiple child classes implement abstract methods, and runtime polymorphism is achieved using a single Animal reference to call different behaviors dynamically.”